# Canvas light dashboard (all workspaces)

Whenever you **create or edit** a `.canvas.tsx` file — this repo, any other workspace, or a new canvas — use this UI. Do not invent a new palette. Do not use `useHostTheme()` or SDK `Text`/`Stat` theme tones as the only color (they go white-on-white in dark IDE).

Keep the canvas **data** unchanged when restyling. If the canvas uses `useCanvasState`, keep the same state keys so ticks are not lost.

## UI principles

- White/light canvas only. Black/dark text everywhere.
- Dashboard hierarchy, not a document: **hero → metrics → run-now → tables → future/footer**.
- Tables are for comparison-heavy information only.
- Run-now is the primary interaction (commands, checks, or the next action).
- Future gates stay compact and collapsible.
- No dark themes, no gradients, no box-shadows, no emojis, no invisible white-on-white text.

## Required imports

Import **only** from `cursor/canvas`. Never import SDK `Text`. Skip `Checkbox` / `useCanvasState` if there are no checks. Add `BarChart` / `LineChart` only when you need a chart. Prefer local `MetricCard` over SDK `Stat`.

```tsx
import {
  Callout,
  Checkbox,
  Divider,
  Grid,
  H1,
  H2,
  H3,
  Pill,
  Row,
  Stack,
  Stat,
  Table,
  useCanvasState,
} from "cursor/canvas";
```

## Copy into every canvas (tokens + helpers)

```tsx
const BG = "#F6F7F9";
const CARD = "#FFFFFF";
const TEXT = "#111827";
const TEXT_MUTED = "#5B6472";
const BORDER = "#E2E6EB";
const BORDER_SOFT = "#EEF0F3";
const NAVY = "#172033";
const GREEN = "#16845B";
const GREEN_BG = "#EAF7F1";
const AMBER = "#9A6500";
const AMBER_BG = "#FFF6DE";
const RED = "#B42318";
const RED_BG = "#FFF0EE";
const BLUE = "#2457D6";
const BLUE_BG = "#EEF3FF";

const page = {
  minHeight: "100%",
  padding: 28,
  background: BG,
  color: TEXT,
  boxSizing: "border-box",
} as const;

const card = {
  background: CARD,
  color: TEXT,
  border: `1px solid ${BORDER}`,
  borderRadius: 14,
  overflow: "hidden",
  boxSizing: "border-box",
} as const;

const body = {
  color: TEXT,
  background: "transparent",
  fontSize: 14,
  lineHeight: 1.5,
  margin: 0,
} as const;

const muted = {
  color: TEXT_MUTED,
  background: "transparent",
  fontSize: 12,
  lineHeight: 1.45,
  margin: 0,
} as const;

function Text({
  children,
  size = 14,
  weight = 400,
  color = TEXT,
}: {
  children: string;
  size?: number;
  weight?: number;
  color?: string;
}) {
  return (
    <span
      style={{
        color,
        background: "transparent",
        fontSize: size,
        fontWeight: weight,
        lineHeight: 1.45,
      }}
    >
      {children}
    </span>
  );
}

function P({ children, small = false }: { children: string; small?: boolean }) {
  return <p style={small ? muted : body}>{children}</p>;
}

function Badge({
  children,
  tone = "neutral",
}: {
  children: string;
  tone?: "success" | "warning" | "danger" | "blue" | "neutral";
}) {
  const styles = {
    success: { bg: GREEN_BG, fg: GREEN, border: "#CDEBDD" },
    warning: { bg: AMBER_BG, fg: AMBER, border: "#F1DE9D" },
    danger: { bg: RED_BG, fg: RED, border: "#F1C8C3" },
    blue: { bg: BLUE_BG, fg: BLUE, border: "#D5DFFF" },
    neutral: { bg: "#F1F3F5", fg: TEXT_MUTED, border: BORDER },
  }[tone];

  return (
    <span
      style={{
        display: "inline-flex",
        alignItems: "center",
        gap: 6,
        padding: "5px 9px",
        borderRadius: 999,
        background: styles.bg,
        color: styles.fg,
        border: `1px solid ${styles.border}`,
        fontSize: 12,
        fontWeight: 700,
        lineHeight: 1,
        whiteSpace: "nowrap",
      }}
    >
      {children}
    </span>
  );
}

function MetricCard({
  value,
  label,
  tone = "neutral",
}: {
  value: string;
  label: string;
  tone?: "success" | "blue" | "neutral";
}) {
  const accent = tone === "success" ? GREEN : tone === "blue" ? BLUE : NAVY;
  return (
    <div style={{ ...card, padding: 16 }}>
      <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 8, marginBottom: 10 }}>
        <div style={{ width: 7, height: 7, borderRadius: 50, background: accent }} />
        <Text size={11} weight={700} color={TEXT_MUTED}>
          {label.toUpperCase()}
        </Text>
      </div>
      <Text size={26} weight={750} color={TEXT}>
        {value}
      </Text>
    </div>
  );
}

function ComparisonTable({
  headers,
  rows,
}: {
  headers: string[];
  rows: string[][];
}) {
  return (
    <Table
      framed
      striped
      stickyHeader
      style={{ ...card, borderRadius: 12 }}
      headers={headers.map((h) => (
        <span
          style={{
            color: TEXT,
            background: "#F8F9FA",
            fontSize: 12,
            fontWeight: 750,
          }}
        >
          {h}
        </span>
      ))}
      rows={rows.map((row) =>
        row.map((cell) => (
          <span
            style={{
              color: TEXT,
              background: CARD,
              fontSize: 12,
              lineHeight: 1.45,
            }}
          >
            {cell}
          </span>
        )),
      )}
    />
  );
}
```

Wrap the default export in `<div style={page}>`. Surfaces use `style={card}`. `H1`/`H2`/`H3` always get `style={{ color: TEXT }}`. H1 may be 30px; metric values 26px.

## Checkbox

`<Checkbox checked={...} onChange={...} />` — **no `label` prop**. Put the label in local `Text` beside it. Stop propagation on the checkbox wrapper. Do not pass `key` onto custom components that reject it — wrap in `<div key=…>`.

## Layout

1. **Hero** — white card: badges, `H1`, one `P`, optional overall progress.
2. **Metrics** — `Grid columns={4}` of `MetricCard`.
3. **Run now** — the only group that should be actively used today (commands or `CheckList`).
4. **ComparisonTable** — routes, decisions, scorecards. Not a wall of paragraphs.
5. **Future** — after `Divider`, compact collapsible `+`/`−` groups.
6. **Footer** — short confirmation / next step on `#FBFCFD`.

Optional: `ProgressBar`, `CheckList`, `GroupCard`, `CompactFutureGate` as in the Milestone 01 QA canvas. Copy those patterns when the canvas has checks; do not copy that canvas’s TripSource QA items into unrelated canvases.

## Forbidden

- `useHostTheme()`, `canvasTokensLight` as the only text color, SDK `Text tone="secondary"`.
- Dark page backgrounds or light-gray-on-dark body text.
- Document-only walls of paragraphs when a metric + table would do.
- Emojis, gradients, box-shadows.
- Checkbox `label` prop.
